# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and deployed to Linux.
# Without this file, shell scripts and container files could be committed with
# CRLF, and on the VM the shebang line becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" — which
# fails with the famously unhelpful:
#     bash: /opt/ems/deploy/ops/backup-verify.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter
# Every ops script (backups, restore rehearsal, TLS reload) would stop running,
# and cron failures are silent by nature.
#
# `text eol=lf` forces LF in the repo AND in the working copy for these types,
# regardless of any individual developer's autocrlf setting.

* text=auto

# Anything executed on Linux must be LF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.ini       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers stay CRLF.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
